# Line endings and the byte-identical core
#
# `greatwall-agent/` is shipped byte-identical to the original Antigravity plugin
# and `core-manifest.sha256` hashes those exact bytes. With `core.autocrlf=true`
# (the default on Windows) a clone would rewrite LF to CRLF and make
# `node tools/verify-core.mjs` fail through no fault of the package, so Git must
# never translate line endings for that tree.
#
# Everything else is ordinary text stored with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
greatwall-agent/** -text
core-manifest.sha256 -text
